# Exporting the database

```bash
./manage.py dumpdata --exclude auth.permission --exclude contenttypes users > users_20230306.json
./manage.py dumpdata --exclude auth.permission --exclude contenttypes regulatory_data > regulatory_data_20230306.json
```

# Importing the data

If you want to clear hte current database and load the new data from the fixtures,
start with a flush

```bash
docker compose -f production.yml run --rm django \
    python manage.py flush
```

first load the users

```bash
/entrypoint python manage.py loaddata yeastregulatorydb/fixtures/users_20240730.json
```

There is a problem importing the data when using a one-to-many relationship. Hence, this
must happen in 2 steps. See

https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/33582

for discussion.

To load the data in this database, first load the tables that do not have one-to-many
dependencies (bindingconcatenated and anything that is related to it)

## Loading fixtures

```bash
docker compose -f production.yml run --rm django \
    python manage.py loaddata \
    /app/yeastregulatorydb/fixtures/users_20250505.json
```

```bash
/entrypoint python manage.py loaddata -v \
  -e regulatory_data.bindingconcatenated \
  -e regulatory_data.bindingmanualqc \
  -e regulatory_data.promotersetsig \
  -e regulatory_data.dto \
  -e regulatory_data.univariatemodels \
  -e regulatory_data.rankresponse \
  yeastregulatorydb/fixtures/regulatory_data_20240730.json
```

Then, exclude the other tables and load bindingconcatenated and its relations

```bash
/entrypoint python manage.py loaddata -v \
  -e regulatory_data.binding \
  -e regulatory_data.callingcardsbackground \
  -e regulatory_data.chrmap \
  -e regulatory_data.datasource \
  -e regulatory_data.expression \
  -e regulatory_data.expressionmanualqc \
  -e regulatory_data.fileformat \
  -e regulatory_data.genomicfeature \
  -e regulatory_data.promoterset \
  -e regulatory_data.regulator \
  yeastregulatorydb/fixtures/regulatory_data_20240730.json
```

or if through the image as a `run` command

```bash
docker compose -f production.yml run \
    -v $(pwd)/yeastregulatorydb/fixtures:/fixtures \
    --rm django  \
    python manage.py loaddata  /fixtures/users_20250520.json


docker compose -f production.yml run \
    -v $(pwd)/yeastregulatorydb/fixtures:/fixtures \
    --rm django \
    python manage.py loaddata \
    -e regulatory_data.bindingconcatenated \
    -e regulatory_data.bindingmanualqc \
    -e regulatory_data.promotersetsig \
    -e regulatory_data.dto \
    -e regulatory_data.univariatemodels \
    -e regulatory_data.rankresponse \
    /fixtures/regulatory_data_20250520.json

docker compose -f production.yml run \
    -v $(pwd)/yeastregulatorydb/fixtures:/fixtures \
    --rm django \
    python manage.py loaddata \
    -e regulatory_data.binding \
    -e regulatory_data.callingcardsbackground \
    -e regulatory_data.chrmap \
    -e regulatory_data.datasource \
    -e regulatory_data.expression \
    -e regulatory_data.expressionmanualqc \
    -e regulatory_data.fileformat \
    -e regulatory_data.genomicfeature \
    -e regulatory_data.promoterset \
    -e regulatory_data.regulator \
    /fixtures/regulatory_data_20250520.json
```

